is strongly associated with higher care needs, particularly intensive formal care. While both physically and cognitively impaired individuals rely heavily on informal care, cognitively impaired individuals receive substantially more hours of care. Total LTC costs amount to $35.3 billion (1.66% of GDP), with cognitively impaired individuals accounting for the largest share of expenditures. Informal care represents a greater financial burden than formal care across all groups. The findings highlight significant unmet care needs and underscore the urgent necessity of policy reforms and healthy ageing strategies to ensure LTC sustainability.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;qRAen7uL2WdvqaJRyRC2MCy7h6CYl-6ohLsNVwgyDD0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx€Cognitive Aging and Long-Term Care in Italy -- by Agar Brugiavini, Ludovico Carrino, Gloria Moroni, Rinaldo Naci, Giacomo Pasiniƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ZCAlyRM6fZ9UlVvyp9KbUbvte1yoQ-oR7vzI_bayxk8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;jyz5JLiBFp7SmvISjdWU_tXYNeo2RT1zfCkojBJCO0Uƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx*https://www.nber.org/papers/w35441#fromrssƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;haKrZMnNqUfVn1Y-BlvUidnN_SVPKhFOwUR9W6bNctEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx`cognitive-aging-and-long-term-care-in-italy-by-agar-brugiavini-ludovico-carrino-gloria-moroni-riƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;oc0dL3U1eUVFIwyVYZvMNOzpVOYznD0piiOA9nkMhTIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwSyndicationSourceBundleƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0S-t82x8zmid9rRNJh